/* A rule with two function parameters f and f_2, in a program with a
   coercion.  The reduction's coercion problem gives each function parameter
   a second copy; when the copy of f was named f_2 it took the name of the
   other parameter. The program is true: the coercion holds (it coerces a
   copy of the input, a list of a, to q0) and the output is a list of a. */
%BEGING
Main x -> G Id Id x.
G f f_2 x -> f (f_2 (H (coerce q0 (Copy x)))).
H y -> case y of
  a y' => a (H y')
| e => e.
Id y -> y.
Copy x -> case x of
  a x' => a (Copy x')
| e => e.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
q0 a -> q0.
q0 e -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
Main : q0 -> q0.
%ENDT
